From 8810cdfa16f7b0157b66b133c4583460e8cfaef8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 17:50:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Preserve SQLite fixture semantics under runtime
 custody auditing

Why: guard installation eagerly read schema, retaining a reader and rejecting intentionally corrupt or locked fixtures; backup-to-memory lost observed trigger custody. Custom connection wrappers also changed class identity and bypassed their authorizer composition. Session fixture provenance must outlive copied homes.

Proof: new regressions RED (4 failed/28 passed, then 2 interface failures); resolved installation without SQL, lazy exact observed trigger definitions and explicit cursor closure, stable class wrappers and native authorizer composition. All 33 formerly failing CI files GREEN: 919 passed, 0 failed, 5 skipped, retries0. Runtime observer remains test-only; no source-text completeness claim or protocol activation.
